---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import CompareByRegion from '../components/CompareByRegion.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import MedicalMap from '../components/MedicalMap.astro';
import { countries } from '../data/index.js';
import fs from 'node:fs';

// Medical costs, topic hub. Gathers every live medical-costs spoke, the same aggregation
// money-scams, staying-connected and the other family hubs use, so each health-wave batch
// surfaces here automatically with no edit to this page. Gathered by SPOKE SLUG rather
// than by topic, deliberately: check-health.mjs allows health-topic spokes outside the
// medical-costs family to exist (and notes them for disclosure review), and this hub is
// the family, not the topic. Checked Aug 2026.
//
// The exposure map renders ON this hub rather than on a page of its own, which is the
// opposite call to the one hotel-tax-map.astro documents, and the difference is the
// reasoning, not an oversight: that map was added above an EXISTING hub that already
// answered its query in its opening lines and ranked on it, so the map would have pushed
// a proven answer below the fold. This hub is new, the map IS its answer, and the brief
// asked for exactly this shape. If the map later earns its own screenshot-and-link URL,
// the component lifts out the way HotelTaxMap did.

const flagDir = process.cwd() + '/public/flags/';
const flagSrc = (slug) => fs.existsSync(flagDir + slug + '.svg') ? '/flags/' + slug + '.svg' : '/flags/world.svg';

const spokes = countries
  .filter(c => c.live)
  .flatMap(c => (c.spokes || [])
    .filter(s => s.slug === 'medical-costs' && s.live !== false)
    .map(s => ({ h1: s.h1, lede: s.lede, spokeSlug: s.slug, country: c.name, countrySlug: c.slug, checkedISO: s.checkedISO })))
  .sort((a, b) => a.country.localeCompare(b.country));

// The hero stamp uses the OLDEST check across the spokes on purpose, the same
// weakest-link promise staying-connected makes: a freshness claim on an aggregate page
// is only as good as its least recently checked member.
const dates = spokes.map(s => s.checkedISO).filter(Boolean).sort();
const stampMonth = dates.length
  ? new Date(dates[0] + 'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleString('en-US', { month: 'short', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })
  : '';
---
<Base
  title="Medical costs abroad, for US travelers: what happens to your money, country by country"
  description="Your US health plan and Medicare almost certainly pay nothing abroad. What happens next depends on the country: some bill you the full non-resident rate, some treat you free until you are admitted, some want a deposit first, and in some the real cost is the flight out. Mapped and written up, country by country, each claim sourced on its own page.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="wrap">

    <Hero
      img="/hero/medical-costs.jpg"
      alt="Illustration of a hand holding a travel card toward a coastal town across calm water"
      eyebrow="Medical costs abroad"
      title="Getting sick abroad is a money question. Here is the honest map of it."
      stamp={stampMonth ? "Checked " + stampMonth : undefined}
      slim />

    <section class="mc-intro">
      <p class="mc-lede">Start from the fact that reorganises everything: Medicare pays essentially nothing outside the United States, and most US health plans pay little or nothing abroad. So the useful question is not whether you are covered, it is what the country you are standing in does with an uncovered visitor. The answer has a small number of honest shapes, and they are worth knowing before you choose what to insure.</p>
      <p class="mc-lede mc-lede2">Some countries bill you the full non-resident rate in an excellent system. One treats you free at the door and charges you the moment you are admitted. One covers your accident and not your illness. Some want money before they will treat you. And in some, the bill that matters is not the ward at all, it is the flight to a country that can treat you. The map below colours each country by which of those is true there, in the words of that country's own page, and each page tells the fuller story.</p>
    </section>

    <MedicalMap />

    <section class="mc-sec">
      <h2>Country by country</h2>
      <p class="mc-note">The full write-up for each country: who the system is for, what a visitor actually pays, how payment works on the ground, and the one sentence worth carrying. Each one lives in that country's guide and is checked and dated on its own page.</p>
      <div class="mc-panel">
        {spokes.map(s => (
          <a class="mc-spoke" href={'/' + s.countrySlug + '/' + s.spokeSlug}>
            <span class="mc-spoke-c"><span class="mc-flag"><img src={flagSrc(s.countrySlug)} alt="" width="22" height="16" loading="lazy" /></span>{s.country}</span>
            <span class="mc-spoke-h">{s.h1}</span>
            <span class="mc-spoke-d">{s.lede}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="mc-keep">Every structural claim on these pages, who the public system covers, what a non-resident is charged, what is required before treatment, is checked against a primary source, State Department and embassy medical pages, the health authority or the scheme itself, and dated on the country's page. Where a routine-care price could not be sourced to that standard, the page says so by name rather than printing a guess, which is why most of these pages carry no price at all. This page prices nothing and diagnoses nothing: if something looks serious, get to care first and deal with the money afterwards. For how a trip's everyday money works, see <a href="/cash-or-card">cash or card by country</a>, and for the charges that land on a hotel bill, <a href="/hotel-taxes-and-fees">hotel taxes and fees</a>. More on how we work is on our <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a>.</p>

    <CompareByRegion />
  </main>
  <Footer />

  <style>
    .mc-intro{max-width:720px;margin:24px 0 0}
    .mc-lede{font-size:18px;color:#3B4A46;line-height:1.55;margin:0}
    .mc-lede2{font-size:16px;color:var(--muted);margin:12px 0 0}
    .mc-sec{margin:38px 0}
    .mc-sec h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(21px,3.2vw,27px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px}
    .mc-note{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5;max-width:720px}
    .mc-panel{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--card);box-shadow:var(--shadow);overflow:hidden}
    .mc-spoke{display:block;padding:15px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color .15s ease}
    .mc-spoke:last-child{border-bottom:0}
    .mc-spoke:hover{background:var(--paper)}
    .mc-spoke-c{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 5px}
    .mc-flag{display:inline-flex;line-height:0;flex:none}
    .mc-flag img{width:22px;height:16px;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid var(--line);object-fit:cover;display:block}
    .mc-spoke-h{display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:16.5px;color:var(--teal-deep);line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 3px}
    .mc-spoke:hover .mc-spoke-h{text-decoration:underline}
    .mc-spoke-d{display:block;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}
    .mc-keep{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:18px;margin:30px 0 40px;max-width:720px}
    .mc-keep a{color:var(--teal-deep);font-weight:500;text-decoration:none}
    .mc-keep a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
    @media (max-width:560px){
      .mc-lede{font-size:16.5px}
      .mc-spoke{padding:14px 15px}
    }
  </style>
</Base>
